      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T00:50:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interrupting Thread is discouraged. I don\u0027t think that stopping due to the no Wi-FI worth doing so especially because it happens when user does something (e.g. Turn off Wi-Fi or moving to somewhere else)\n\nReferences:\n - Internal [Java Practice](https://engdoc.corp.google.com/eng/doc/devguide/java/practices/interruption.md?cl\u003dhead#dont-interrupt) says almost never interrupt another thread.\n - [Effective Java](go/ej3e-78) also says \u0027A recommended way to stop one thread from another is to have the first thread poll a boolean field that is initially false but can be set to true by the second thread to indicate that the first thread is to stop itself\u0027",
      "parentUuid": "97ab6556_0a202ba6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 350,
